    {
      "question": "The Water fund issued 580,000 of debt and paid 560,000 of refinanced principal, both printed under Nonoperating Revenues (Expenditures) of the proprietary statement. Should this refinancing stay as a business-type receipt and debt-service disbursement, or be treated as financing (debt_proceeds / other_financing)?",
      "amount": 580000,
      "recorded_as": "business-type receipt 'Issuance of debt' 580,000 (Debt Proceeds) and disbursement 'Debt service principal refinanced' 560,000 (Debt Service principal), per the printed-section rule",
      "source_page": 7
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Modified cash basis village audit (FY ended 9/30/2022). Governmental lines from the governmental funds statement Total Governmental Funds column (pp4-5); fund balance roll-forward 315,991 + 410,261 - 375,084 - transfers 9,777 (printed net in Total column: General +30,000, ARPA -39,777) + insurance proceeds 13,543 = 354,934 (p5). Governmental cash: governmental funds Cash 92,154 (2021 column 85,320), certificates of deposit 135,352 (2021: 134,508) as investments (p3); cash held by county treasurer 5,183 (Street) is a separate line, not in ending_cash (as FY2023). Statement 'Intergovernmental' 198,491 kept as one line though it includes ARPA grant 36,813. Business-type lines from the modified cash proprietary statement Total column (p7); net position 581,541 -> 569,945; transfers net +9,777 (Electric -30,000, Sewer +39,777). Water fund refinancing (Issuance of debt 580,000 / Debt service principal refinanced 560,000) printed under nonoperating revenues (expenditures), recorded as receipt/disbursement lines (see decision_needed). The Statement of Activities (p2) shows business-type expenditures 923,686, i.e. the proprietary total 943,686 net of the 20,000 net refinancing. Proprietary cash flow statement (pp8-9) printed but proprietary left null as in FY2023/FY2024 (modified cash). Balance sheet = government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1) because the governmental funds statement (p3) carries due from/to other funds rather than the internal balance. Detail: General Fund by department (p12), Street (p13), Fitness Center (p14), ARPA (p15); utility funds have no detail (as FY2023/FY2024); the all-funds budgetary comparison (p10, one combined column) and General Fund asset balances by department (p11) are not recorded to avoid double counting. Statement capital outlay 8,263 is Swimming Pool 4,872 + Park 3,391, both under the Culture and Recreation heading (p12). Read pages 1-15 of 15"
}
